            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    To Gaius Valerius Marianus, son of Gaius, of tribe Papiria, having obtained all the honours at Tridentum, flamen of Roma and Augustus, quinquennial prefect, augur, appointed to the grain supply of the Third Italic Legion, member of the priesthood for the sacred rites at Tusculum, selected judge of the tribunician decury, decurion at Brixia, curator of the public affairs of the Mantuans, honoured with a public horse, prefect of engineers, patron of the colony. [This was] erected at public expense.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>This is the same Gaius Valerius Marianus in AE 1990.422</p> 
            </div>
